WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.347
Chat A P I's commonly separate messages into roles.

00:00:04.347 --> 00:00:11.417
The system role defines behavior or high-level rules, the user role contains a request,

00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:15.737
and assistant messages represent earlier model responses.

00:00:15.737 --> 00:00:19.652
These roles help preserve conversation structure across turns.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:23.952
The system message is not magical security.

00:00:23.952 --> 00:00:30.160
It is part of the model input, so real permissions still need to be enforced by application code.
